#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
patch_L334_7_dashboard_gallery_web_20260918.py -- ORRERY repo.

Run: save this file in the ORRERY repo ROOT (next to
palomas_orrery_dashboard.py), open it in VS Code and click Run.
Or:  python patch_L334_7_dashboard_gallery_web_20260918.py

A patch is run from its repository's ROOT and filed in documentation/ AFTER
it has run. Filed first and run second, it stops with one line, writes
nothing, and the push goes out without it.

Built on orrery 709e16ad284b77c6f31eb3cb69e89ccfb43cc7cc
at https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery
(gallery d3e90bae14f373a2a99aa889b8ff01f0a72adc4e)

WHAT IT DOES (one file, palomas_orrery_dashboard.py):

  MOVES Exhibit Store Editor out of Developer Tools and into Gallery &
  Web, beside Gallery Studio and Gallery Editor, on Tony's second
  thought of 2026-09-18.

  ADDS two buttons for gallery checkers that had none: Store Writer
  Suite and Store Editor Suite.

  SORTS Gallery & Web the way Developer Tools was sorted on 2026-09-12,
  which is Tony's own ruling applied to the other group: the offline
  maintenance run first, then the checkers it covers, indented and
  alphabetical, then the live run, then the standalone tools,
  alphabetical. A FLAT alphabetical sort was the literal instruction and
  would have scattered the indented checkers among the standalone tools,
  which is what the indent is there to prevent -- so the alphabetising
  happens WITHIN each half. Say the word and it becomes flat.

  Every entry keeps its own source text, comments included. The patch
  reorders the lines; it does not rewrite them.

  One line is added to the module's change log at the top.

WHAT IS STILL MISSING, and it is not in this patch. The gallery runner
has 14 checkers and the dashboard now has buttons for 10. The four
without are Feature renderers, Page framing, Sun shells and Earth scene
geometry -- all Node, and this dashboard launches everything with
Python. Hover Budget has a button only because someone wrote
documentation/run_hover_budget.py to wrap it. Four more wrappers, or one
launcher that knows about Node, would close it. Worth a ledger line
rather than a patch tonight.

SAFE TO RUN BEFORE THE EDITOR EXISTS. exhibit_store_editor.py and
test_exhibit_store_editor.py land in the GALLERY repo in a later push.
Until then those two buttons log "Not found: ..." in the status panel
and do nothing else. Store Writer Suite works now.

THEN (Tony): python orrery_maintenance_run.py, then move this script into
documentation/, commit and push.

FAILURE: a single ERROR: or ANCHOR FAIL line, and NOTHING is written.
Undo is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written September 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.
"""
